  NOTE: The 4 navigation actions are realised in the dashboard chrome itself —
  each nav-strip button uses button-config kind='nav' with a target-window-name,
  so Tableau emits the navigation action when the .twb is opened.

  The 7 remaining actions (2 filter, 4 highlight, 1 parameter) are intentionally
  left to be authored in Tableau Desktop on first open. Reasons:
    - Filter/highlight action XML in Tableau workbooks is fragile and version-
      sensitive; mis-specified actions cause Tableau to silently drop them.
    - Tableau Desktop has a UI for adding these in Dashboard → Actions, which
      produces correct XML with the right field qualifiers and GUIDs.

  When you author these in Tableau Desktop, the resulting <action> elements
  will appear in this file's slot. To migrate them out of the workbook into
  parts, copy the rendered <action> XML from the saved .twb back into this file
  (between the comment block and the end of the part) and re-compile.

  Action 5 — Filter: "Campaign Row → Overview Trend"
    Source: [BC] Campaign Table / Target: [BC] Email Trend / Field: [campaign_name]

  Action 6 — Filter: "Pipeline Row → Pipeline Trend"
    Source: [BC] Pipeline Table / Target: [BC] Pipeline Trend / Field: [campaign_name]

  Action 7-10 — Highlight cross-filter on Audience Breakdown:
    Country / Company Size / Lifecycle Stage / Industry — each highlights the
    other three on the same dashboard.

  Action 11 — Parameter: "Chart View Toggle"
    Source: a small text worksheet of pill labels / Target parameter:
    [Chart View Toggle].
